# mulder 1.5.10 with tools that do the work Haiku leaves undone (EXP-004):
# the limits carried to the analyst (as in mulder-1.5.10-limits-to-analyst);
# run_hashdeep checking the EWF acquisition hash with ewfverify;
# analyze_disk_pcaps finding captures by header, summarizing HTTP hosts and
# user agents and naming the file's path; get_windows_system_profile with
# the installed programs; get_recycle_bin; run_clamav scanning the files
# inside a disk image; get_completed_results returning source names; and
# the tools a disk image needs added to the first plan when the planner
# leaves them out. Candidate fixes, not upstream.
BASE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/calebevans/mulder:1.5.10@sha256:b14737ebf9c4cb155e00ebe617d615db25840bdc55a3ca619c99647131550cfb
REF=951e639e9e1a2af84157ba765f6d9b4b96124177   # v1.5.10
PATCHES="disk-pcap-no-results-scope.patch batch-results-status-message.patch limits-reach-analyst.patch haiku-tool-assists.patch haiku-tool-assists-2.patch haiku-tool-assists-3.patch"
